{"message_id":"c5a7e3f5-f1c8-4a21-b523-d1a20dbe04a3","timestamp":"2026-05-08T17:04:25.977969Z","version":"1.0","source_id":"jarvis","event_type":"command","project":null,"correlation_id":"368f9149-16fd-4f4b-9b33-68690f847f33","payload":{"command":"architect_explore","args":{"question":"Is adding a Claude Opus 4.7 escalation tool (triggered by low local-confidence on safety-critical requests, bound by per-session budget) architecturally sound given ADR-ARCH-001's local-first invariant that explicitly keeps cloud LLMs out of the supervisor hot path?","context":"ADR-ARCH-001 commits Jarvis to local-first inference via llama-swap. Cloud LLMs are explicitly out of the supervisor hot path. The proposal wants to introduce cloud as an escalation path for safety-critical/high-stakes scenarios when local confidence is low, with a per-session budget cap. This would modify the supervisor contract to conditionally route to cloud."},"correlation_id":"368f9149-16fd-4f4b-9b33-68690f847f33"}}
{"message_id":"ccfc7b78-72d3-4352-a650-614555aa86f7","timestamp":"2026-05-08T17:07:03.165232Z","version":"1.0","source_id":"jarvis","event_type":"command","project":null,"correlation_id":"8df345b4-7b47-4214-8ae3-959aac5252e4","payload":{"command":"architect_align","args":{"context":"ADR-ARCH-001 (jarvis) commits jarvis to local-first inference via llama-swap. Cloud LLMs are explicitly prohibited from the supervisor hot path. All reasoning must run locally on the GB10 box via the qwen36-workhorse model. The ADR was written to lock in the marginal-cost-zero economics that the 2026 Software Factory talk depends on.","proposal":"Add a Claude Opus 4.7 escalation tool that the supervisor can invoke when its local reasoner reports low confidence on safety-critical or high-stakes user requests. The escalation is bound by a per-session budget cap and is opt-in only when the user explicitly asks for a frontier opinion.","question":"Is this proposal architecturally sound given ADR-ARCH-001 local-first invariant? What changes to the ADR or to the supervisor contract would the architect need to see for this to be aligned?"},"correlation_id":"8df345b4-7b47-4214-8ae3-959aac5252e4"}}
